Fix AIKIDO-2026-310861 (CWE-843 type confusion via thenable assimilation in
the seroval core deserializer) for the seroval-plugins package.

The vulnerable code path lives in the SEPARATE `seroval` core package
(packages/seroval/src/core/context/deserializer.ts): a reconstructed Promise
was settled directly with whatever value a Promise/PromiseSuccess/PromiseFailure
node deserialized to. A crafted payload could make that value a *thenable*
(an object exposing a callable `then`); native Promise resolution then
assimilates it and invokes the attacker-controlled `then` callback during
deserialization. Upstream fixed this in seroval@1.6.2 (commit f1ffcc9) by
guarding the settle paths with an isThennable() check.

`seroval-plugins` ships NONE of that core source (its published npm tarball
contains only package.json, web/*.ts and dist/**). It merely rides on top of
the version-locked `seroval` core. The correct, artifact-applicable remediation
is therefore to raise the pinned/peer `seroval` dependency floor to the fixed
core release so any install of seroval-plugins resolves a patched deserializer.

